course: dictionary
lesson: 191
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word airline has two. «For the same distance, flying on a big airline is much safer than going by car.» Here an airline is a company that flies planes with passengers and goods.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is right. Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If it is about flying, tickets and passengers, the company meaning fits. If it is about a diver under the sea, an air line means a pipe that carries air down to them.
explain: Check your choice by swapping the meaning into the sentence. Does «a company that flies planes» still make sense? Then try the other meaning. The one that fits is the right one.
fact: An airline is a company that flies planes carrying passengers or goods to different places.
fact: An air line can also be a pipe or tube that carries air, for example to a diver.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is read correctly by looking at the words around it.
fact: «Airline ticket», «airline pilot» and «airline food» all use the company meaning.
fact: A child flying alone, an unaccompanied minor, stays with the airline staff member who looks after them.
exercise: «For the same distance, flying on a big airline is much safer than going by car.» What is an airline in this sentence? | A pipe that carries air to a diver | A type of bird | A road for cars | *A company that flies planes with passengers
exercise: «A boy flying alone from Dallas to Denver stays with the airline staff member who looks after him.» What does the staff member do? | Carries his bags to the sea | *Looks after him until his grandma meets him | Gives him a tube to breathe through | Flies the plane to Denver
exercise: A diver breathes through an air line that runs down from the boat. What does air line mean here? | A line drawn on a map | A ticket for a flight | A company that flies planes | *A tube that carries air
test: «The airline pilot waved from the cockpit.» Which meaning of airline fits? | A tube of toothpaste | A flight number | *A company that flies planes | A pipe that carries air
test: «The diver pumped air down an air line to the water.» What does air line mean? | A tube of toothpaste | *A pipe or tube that carries air | A flight number | A company that flies planes
exam: «She checked her luggage with the airline before boarding.» Which meaning fits, and how do you know? | A pipe that carries air, because she needed to breathe | It is a spelling mistake, so there is no meaning | *A company that flies planes, because luggage and boarding are about flights | A line drawn on a map, because it is long
